{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791534680,"nonce":"pJnFsP3YD0kv0b8uWluqpXaRTmA=","message":"Milestone committed: 7c81996 Create renderer pipelines and atlases on demand.\n\nTen eagerly built UI pipelines are now cached on first use. Layer bind groups are lazy too, so a single backdrop does not inadvertently compile every layer shader. Text/image atlases are created only when display-list text/images or canvas drawing need them. New passes bind already-allocated record textures; texture growth rebinds existing passes. Explicit shader handles are released after pipeline construction, and old atlas/layer/record views are released on replacement.\n\nVerification on macOS Metal:\n- Full tests/fixtures/render/Pixels.hx passed, including added checks for no eager pipelines/atlases, box+shadow-only first frame, unchanged cached pipelines after record-texture growth. Existing tests introduce canvas, layer effects, glass, images and text in later frames.\n- Geometry/glass (640x440 at 1x) and nested layers (640x480 at 2x) matched the old renderer byte-for-byte across 30 completed frames, 2 fresh processes for each of Ash hybrid/interpreter. GPU validation passed.\n- Simple geometry excluding shadows/backdrops, interpreter mode: physical footprint 94.92/94.99 MiB before versus 61.17/59.31 MiB after. Same RGBA SHA256 3ec6cba74a8dfdb6d61d353c36fb3f19a99eb9982ac39a459f7e98eb8b7967f9. proc_pid_rusage measurement after GPU completion, no concurrent render tests.\n- Geometry with glass: hybrid after 105.7-135.5 MiB (variable JIT activity), interpreter 100.6-100.9 MiB. Nested layers: hybrid 253.7-256.4 MiB, interpreter 202.3-204.8 MiB. Scenes using most effects save less. Do not describe the simple-scene percentage as universal.\n\nWGSL remains static final; first use incurs shader compilation and is then cached per renderer. hlwgpu git-bug 0d9a25c tracks HXSL value-block expansion and compiler/driver memory. No change to xgpu/hlwgpu APIs is needed for this milestone.\n\nLocal raw reports and binary hashes: .ashui/memory-comparison/shader-demand-results.json. Remaining investigation includes scratch textures per layer, complete renderer/scene resource lifetimes, idle wakeups, and Ash AIR/JIT retention (existing Ash reports d0ca1c3, f60b855, 6fde0a9; prior full-program clone bug 6177f7e is already fixed).","files":null}]}